<title>GERMANY: Key economic forecasts from German Wise Men report.</title>
<headline>Key economic forecasts from German Wise Men report.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are key economic data from the 1996/97 annual report of the German government's independent Council of Economic Advisers, also known as the Five Wise Men (figures are real year-on-year percentage changes unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>					 1997     1996     1995</p>
<p> Pan German GDP		    +2.5     +1.5     +1.9</p>
<p> West German GDP		   +2.5     +1.5     +1.6</p>
<p> East German GDP		   +2.25    +2.0     +5.3</p>
<p> Unemployment (millions)	 4.065    3.900    3.612</p>
<p> Consumer price inflation	+1.75    +1.75    +1.8</p>
<p> GDP deflator			+1.5     +1.25    +2.2</p>
<p> Private consumption	     +1.75    +1.75    +1.8</p>
<p> Public consumption		+1.0     +2.75    +2.0</p>
<p> Fixed asset investment	  +1.25    -1.25    +1.5</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>  Capital investment	     +3.5     +0.5     +2.0</p>
<p>  Construction investment	-0.25    -2.25    +1.2</p>
<p> Exports			     +6.75    +3.5     +5.9</p>
<p> Imports			     +4.75    +2.0     +6.4</p>
<p> Productivity			+3.0     +3.5     +3.5</p>
<p>DETAILED GDP FORECASTS:</p>
<p>					 H1 1997 H2 1997 H1 1996 H2 1996</p>
<p> Pan German			  +2.50   +2.25   +0.7    +2.25</p>
<p> West German			 +2.50   +2.25   +0.7    +2.0</p>
<p> East German			 +3.50   +1.0    +0.7    +3.5</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
